title: Proposition 29
---
order: 29
---
short_label: VII.29
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Any prime number is relatively prime to any number which it does not measure.
----
proof:

Let *A* be a prime number, and let it not measure *B.*

I say that *B* and *A* are relatively prime.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="250" height="140" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VII.29 diagram" src="propVII29.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
